<title>USA: SubMicron to have Q3 gain on unit sale.</title>
<headline>SubMicron to have Q3 gain on unit sale.</headline>
<dateline>ALLENTOWN, Pa. 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>SubMicron Systems Corp said Friday it will have a gain of about $2 million in the third quarter from the sale of its Systems Chemistry Inc subsidiary to BOC Group Plc.</p>
<p>SubMicron said it received $20.8 million in cash after the establishment of a reserve account in the amount of $1.5 million to cover potential post closing working capital adjustments.  The proceeds include a subordinated, non-interest bearing loan of $5 million due in three years. As announced on June 30, the company has applied net proceeds, $18.8 million, to its current bank debt obligation.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
